# Squad: union merge for append-only team state files.
#
# .squad/agents/*/history.md and .squad/decisions.md use the custom
# `squad-history` driver instead of plain `union`: union merge cannot
# represent a deletion, so a Scribe condensation (history.md) or archival
# (decisions.md) gets silently undone the next time a branch that forked
# before it is merged (see decisions.md, 2026-08-03, "the merge=union
# condensation defect"). `squad-history` keeps union merge's no-conflict
# guarantee for concurrent agent appends but respects whichever side
# removed content. Requires running
# .squad/tools/setup-merge-drivers.ps1 once per clone/worktree -- driver
# commands live in .git/config, which git never versions.
.squad/decisions.md merge=squad-history
.squad/agents/*/history.md merge=squad-history
.squad/log/** merge=union
.squad/orchestration-log/** merge=union
.squad/rai/audit-trail.md merge=union
.squad/fact-checker/audit-trail.md merge=union

# Shell scripts must stay LF-terminated: a CRLF .sh fails under WSL as
#   cd: $'...\r': No such file or directory
*.sh text eol=lf

# `evidence/` deliberately has NO merge driver, and must not get `union`.
# `evidence/retired_proof_keys.json` is the proof-retirement register: retiring
# a key is a DELETION of a claim's exemption, and union merge cannot represent
# a deletion -- it would resurrect a retired key the next time a branch that
# forked before the retirement is merged, and the census would then read the
# resurrected row as still-exempt with nobody having signed for it. This is the
# same defect that forced `squad-history` on .squad/decisions.md, one directory
# over. Evidence conflicts are meant to stop a merge and be resolved by the
# owner named in the register's `owner` field (issue #3, 2026-08-05).

# Replay fixtures for the cleanroom index-URL privacy control are CONTENT-ADDRESSED:
# ci/fixtures/cleanroom-redaction/manifest.json pins a sha256 per fixture. They are the
# exact module bytes two rejected heads of PR #57 shipped, kept as evidence because a
# squash landing deletes the branch and the refs with it. Mark them binary so no
# line-ending translation can touch them on checkout -- the digest is the whole point.
ci/fixtures/cleanroom-redaction/*.pysrc -text
